[[File:Shopping (Beta 25.0).png|thumb|264x264px|Beta 25.0]]
When class spells were added in '''Alpha 3.0''', Shopping costed 4G to make you draw 2 cards. This stayed all the way until '''Beta 6.7''', where its cost dropped to 3G.
[[File:Shopping (Beta 44.0).png|thumb|257x257px|Beta 44.0]]
'''Beta 14.0''' brought changes to the card by changing its effect. Now, it will make you draw a card for every 5 gold you have (including the 3G of Shopping itself, similar to an old [[Mettaton Ex|Mettaton EX]]). So it will fail if you don't have 5G and, when taking in account an empty hand after use, will make you overdraw cards starting from 40G.
[[File:Shopping (Beta 52.1).png|thumb|Btea 52.1]]
'''Beta 22.0''' reworked this card entirely. While the card itself costs 0G, you lose all the gold you currently have to summon a random monster from your deck that has a cost equal to the amount of gold you spent. This was buffed in '''Beta 24.0''' where it now summons a copy of the card, and buffed again in '''Beta 25.0''' where if you don't have a monster with the exact cost, it chooses the most expensive cheaper monster instead.

'''Beta 44.0''' brought its cost back to its original 4G. Its effect got reworked once more. Now, you draw cards until you've drawn a combined cost of 10G or more out of the cards you've drawn or until you have 7 cards in your hand (making you not overdraw at any time). This was changed in '''Beta 52.1''' to making you draw 3 cards with a cost of 5G or lower. '''Beta 54.1''' reduce its cost back down to 3G.

